{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return","id":25163,"title":"What Lunar Charms do you expect will or will not return?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-07T09:25:28-08:00","id":25163,"title":"What Lunar Charms do you expect will or will not return?","content":"I suspect that the space-time Charms of Second Edition will not reappear. That is, such reality-cheating shenanigans as Spreading the Wyld Roots, Moonlight Hunt, Stars Fall Through, Secure Den Prana (and all derivatives) and Blinking Eye of Chaos look to me like they will instead return as Getimian tricks resulting from using their personal, internal Looms of Fate to counter the designs of Heaven's Pattern Spiders. They not only overwrite their personal relationship with gravity (as teased) but potentially other natural laws as well -- space, time, momentum, friction, etc.<br /> <br /> In any case, nothing about &quot;Half-Beast-God Trickster-Witch-Shaman&quot; suggests space-time manipulation to me. I think the &quot;intensely physical&quot; Lunar Exalted will etch their legends into the world with &quot;bestial, inhuman&quot; feats of strength and speed. If those feats are inferior to those of the Solar Exalted, that's nothing we haven't been told before. You don't play a Lunar to be the strongest or fastest hero in the universe, you play to be a hero who is Half-Beast-God.<br /> <br /> As to what tricks the Lunars may have for dealing with the Wyld, I can't say until I know what form the Wyld takes, now that it is no longer a &quot;lava-lamp with infinite numbers of fairies in it&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> We have been told to not expect &quot;illusions&quot;, but rather a trend of Lunars &quot;changing themselves to change the world&quot;. So I'm pretty sure we're not ever going to see a Lunar mirror of Phantom-Conjuring Performance, and also that all disguise-magic will involve physically reshaping the Lunar's appearance rather than layering over false images and sounds. I suspect that Lunars may cause people to see things which are not there through inflicting delusional or hallucinatory <i>insanity </i>rather than fooling the eyes with tricks of light.<br /> <br /> To that end, I don't expect to see Inexplicable Lunar Wonders, River Reflects Desire, Dreams and Expectations Stance, Shifting Penumbra Stance, One Of The Herd, Clover Can't Be Found, the second half of The Spider's Trapdoor, Treasure as Trash Misdirection, or any of those Butterfly Eyes Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be clear, I don't think they were talking about all forms of the Illusion <i>Keyword</i>, since some of those were more about beliefs inflicted through lies and misdirections rather than through sensory illusions. So I still expect to see Perfection of the Mockingbird, Mockingbird Persona Mimicry, Scent of All Nations Attitude, and Falling Leaf Distraction.<br /> <br /> False Burrow Pursuit, Mirror Sight Dismay and Lost Mirror Flight can also make returns so long as the Lunar has to actually speak to his victim with a social action. Oh, and let's not forget brutal traumatizing through Mind-Blanking Terror Technique.<br /> <br /> I also think we can still look forward to sleights of hand, as with Face Of The Moon Concealment, School Becomes Shark Formation, School In The Reeds Technique, Thieving Magpie Prana, the first half of The Spider's Trapdoor, and possibly Rats In The Basement.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think, with the greater emphasis on one's Totem as an inescapable starting point for every Lunar Exalted character, Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick might not necessarily always work by temporarily giving you an egg-implanting stinger. It doesn't quite fit with any but an extremely small selection of Totems, whereas a necromantic entry Charm like this ought to be fairly popular among the Lunar Exalted who want to explore the Trickster-Witch-Shaman part of their Essence.<br /> <br /> On the opposite side of the death/life line of &quot;barbaric magic&quot;, given the hints of greater connections to Gaia, we might be seeing the return of Moon And Earth Song, the Charm which blesses a territory with great fertility.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder, though, if the territory claiming and enchanting Charms will be Essence 5 or even 6+ effects, reflecting that Essence 6+ characters are generally supposed to be sedentary while Essence 5- characters are geared more towards adventuring across the world on a moment's notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T11:30:03-08:00","id":25255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return#post25163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We have been told to not expect &quot;illusions&quot;, but rather a trend of Lunars &quot;changing themselves to change the world&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably one of the most troubling things I've heard about 3rd edition Lunars since illusions have generally been something that I thought fit the Changing Moon Caste like a glove.<br /> Though it really does depend on what &quot;changing themselves to change the world&quot; actually means in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T11:33:04-08:00","id":25262,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope Butterfly Eyes Fist remains, though I can't say the same for all the speedbump Charms before it. It absolutely screams Trickster in a Jackie Chan kinda way and I don't think it's abstract as all that, it's just a feint made supernaturally effective. As if &quot;look over there!&quot; could work and make your target not only look, but jerk his sword sideways into his ally as well. As a Trickster I would hope that the following tricks would work: playing the broken winged bird to draw attention away from something, mischievously compelling someone to chase me, compelling someone to flee from me in terror, entrancing someone with a gaudy display, compelling someone to do something by asking them not to (Brer Rabbit or even &quot;Duck Season! Rabbit Season!&quot;).<br /> <br /> As a Shaman I want to be able to sense and converse with the unseen as well as physically interact with it. Like how cats sometimes pounce on &quot;nothing.&quot; I kinda do think that a Witch's den should be bigger on the inside than the outside though, even if she has to excavate it by hand and claw alone. I also expect her curses to deal with spittle and blood and hair and nails in the old fashioned way. Perhaps like the Shinto demon hunters, spit and hair and blood will be able to ward against, bind, and harm spirits. I also think it would be nice for a Lunar witch to be able to do things like eat the eyes of the dead and see what they saw, but maybe that's reaching too far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T11:57:59-08:00","id":25276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=25255#post25255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably one of the most troubling things I've heard about 3rd edition Lunars since illusions have generally been something that I thought fit the Changing Moon Caste like a glove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing one of the reasons is to better distinguish them from the raksha. And perhaps to make the Lunars seem even more cunning when they trick you without using visual illusions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=25262#post25262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly hope Butterfly Eyes Fist remains, though I can't say the same for all the speedbump Charms before it. It absolutely screams Trickster in a Jackie Chan kinda way and I don't think it's abstract as all that, it's just a feint made supernaturally effective. As if &quot;look over there!&quot; could work and make your target not only look, but jerk his sword sideways into his ally as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll have to see what kind of restrictions 3rd Edition allows us to place on that Charm, as being able to outright dictate your opponent's next move as anything you please always seemed broken to me.<br /> <br /> Personally, I looked at that Charm and had the idea that there might a much more modest Charm you use to &quot;train&quot; your opponent into reacting a certain way.<br /> <br /> Like how a boxer might always lead with a left punch until the final round, and suddenly always lead with his right fist -- his opponent has gotten so deep into the previous groove that he has trouble adjusting to this new tactic. That kind of &quot;training&quot;, only made supernaturally effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a Trickster I would hope that the following tricks would work: playing the broken winged bird to draw attention away from something, mischievously compelling someone to chase me, compelling someone to flee from me in terror, entrancing someone with a gaudy display, compelling someone to do something by asking them not to (Brer Rabbit or even &quot;Duck Season! Rabbit Season!&quot;). </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a Shaman I want to be able to sense and converse with the unseen as well as physically interact with it. Like how cats sometimes pounce on &quot;nothing.&quot; </div> </div> </div>A spirit-seeing Charm is rather mandatory for Charmsets in this setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I kinda do think that a Witch's den should be bigger on the inside than the outside though, even if she has to excavate it by hand and claw alone. </div> </div> </div>I likewise think that something like Secure Den Prana could survive in the form of carving a physical den into the real world. None of this &quot;disappearing into Elsewhere&quot; business, though.<br /> <br /> Maybe Lunars can create Spirit Sanctums, which are vulnerable to the usual methods of finding and invading sanctums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think it would be nice for a Lunar witch to be able to do things like eat the eyes of the dead and see what they saw, but maybe that's reaching too far? </div> </div> </div>That's an Abyssal Charm, but Lunars could possibly have a variation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T16:54:12-08:00","id":51978,"title":"","content":"Do you think Monkey Arm Style will return?<br /> <br /> The hatewheel has expressed contempt for and exasperation with &quot;elastic body&quot; powers, but the hamster has said that something like the elastic body Shintai from Kindred of the East is not out of the question (though he didn't say for which splats).<br /> <br /> Monkey Arm Style does seem problematic for me in regards to the Lunar Exalted. The Alchemical Exalted have an excellent reason for an extending arm feature to NOT include the option to extend one's other appendages or body parts, which allows for it to be a properly self-contained Charm, with an entirely separate cousin Charm that extends the Alchemical's legs. Easy to design, balance and write.<br /> <br /> But unlike the Alchemical Exalted, the Lunar Exalted can easily switch back and forth between forms that technically don't have any arms at all, or at least where their arms would be legs or wings. It's also harder (though admittedly not impossible) to justify why a Lunar Charm which extends an arm (which could be a foreleg) doesn't also extend the Lunar's legs. And a Charm that allows an Exalt to extend both arms and legs is an extremely complicated mess to design, balance and write.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is, I think the Lunar Exalted may already be so variable in form that giving them &quot;elastic body&quot; Charms might not actually over-complicate things. Whereas Exalts who don't have the innate power to easily assume any inhuman form can freely accept such tricks into their arsenal (especially the Liminal and Alchemical Exalted).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:15:41-08:00","id":51990,"title":"","content":"I really liked the feel of the &quot;Butterfly Eyes&quot; charms, even if they weren't Psylocke references...<br /> <br /> Do we know if Knacks are confirmed for 3e, or are those powers going to be Charms again?<br /> <br /> As an aside, do folks really prefer 1E's &quot;totem&quot; to 2E's &quot;spirit shape&quot;, or do you just use them interchangeably?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:29:34-08:00","id":51997,"title":"","content":"Totem is a stronger word, I think. I certainly wouldn't complain if it became the default term again.<br /> For the same reason, I prefer &quot;totemic&quot; to &quot;iconic&quot; when it comes to anima banners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:37:23-08:00","id":51998,"title":"","content":"I prefer Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:06:31-08:00","id":52022,"title":"","content":"For me, I believe that &quot;spirit shape&quot; refers to the basic animal form that you can assume from the start, whereas the Totem is the entire image that your character has built around that shape.<br /> <br /> As an example, Silver Python's Spirit Shape might be a normal-sized python, but his/her <i>Totem </i>is the gigantic, world-spanning serpent that embodies strength, wisdom, patience and flexibility.<br /> <br /> So I guess &quot;Totem&quot; is basically the combination of your Spirit Shape and Caste, with the Favored Attribute and any Totemic Keywords added in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T19:03:15-08:00","id":52067,"title":"","content":"I hope those &quot;turn leaf into money&quot; charms disappear quietly into the night, the only one who don't look silly while using those charms are Raska.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:50:59-08:00","id":52339,"title":"","content":"We'll probably continue to see something like Impressions of Strength. I'd LIKE to see the Butterfly Eyes charms go on, if only better implemented; Butterfly Eyes Tread has some potentially horrific applications, but it's also pretty much a very specific use (&quot;trick a dude into walking into traffic/off a ledge.&quot;), and while there's room for otherworldly and guileful in the Lunar charmsets I'm not sure if that fits particularly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:14:29-08:00","id":52469,"title":"","content":"My personal favourites are things like Hybrid-Body Rearrangement, Wound-Mastering Body Evolution and Flesh-Sculpting Art. Things that play off the adaptability of their shapeshifting abilities and push towards body-horror territory. I dearly hope these make reappearances but I'm worried they won't.<br /> <br /> Motive-Dissecting Eye is a useful and interesting tool and another favourite of mine. Knowing <i>why</i> someone is doing something helps set up all sorts of schemes and can be an excellent tool for figuring out mysteries without just straight up giving you the answer. Again, hoping for a reappearance.<br /> <br /> Lunar Blade Reconfiguration is basically the only part of Lunar craft that I actually like. So long as lunars can still have shape-shifting swords and reconfigurable tools in some form I'll be happy, even if it just becomes an evocation for Moonsilver artifacts or something.<br /> <br /> Command to Fly and False Burrow Pursuit (along with most of the charms leading on from it) I fully expect to see reappear. They're very trickster-ish, not to mention fun. I particularly like that they encourage you to think about using them a little.<br /> <br /> I am looking forward to seeing how they pull off the shaman theme well. There's no doubt in my mind that trickster and warrior will be well served, but shaman has me worried. Just hoping that they get plenty of charms that play into Luna's thematics - she's just as, if not more important to her chosen than the Unconquered Sun is to his in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Hopefully if they're making Totem more important they'll make it easier to actually get the totem you want. Having to start with Essence 3, Stamina 4 and two knacks just to give a No Moon a butterfly totem is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1218,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","user":"Taejix","date":". 01-18-2014, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","name":"Taejix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:31:01-08:00","id":52486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taejix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52469#post52469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal favourites are things like Hybrid-Body Rearrangement, Wound-Mastering Body Evolution and Flesh-Sculpting Art. Things that play off the adaptability of their shapeshifting abilities and push towards body-horror territory. I dearly hope these make reappearances but I'm worried they won't.<br /> <br /> Motive-Dissecting Eye is a useful and interesting tool and another favourite of mine. Knowing <i>why</i> someone is doing something helps set up all sorts of schemes and can be an excellent tool for figuring out mysteries without just straight up giving you the answer. Again, hoping for a reappearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it can be Motive-Dissecting Tongue? &quot;You taste like a liar.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunar Blade Reconfiguration is basically the only part of Lunar craft that I actually like. So long as lunars can still have shape-shifting swords and reconfigurable tools in some form I'll be happy, even if it just becomes an evocation for Moonsilver artifacts or something. </div> </div> </div>I think we got confirmation on that dying earlier than anything else. I heard that it clashed with developer vision for the distinctness of magical weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Command to Fly and False Burrow Pursuit (along with most of the charms leading on from it) I fully expect to see reappear. They're very trickster-ish, not to mention fun. I particularly like that they encourage you to think about using them a little. </div> </div> </div>Neither of them are really all that physical, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am looking forward to seeing how they pull off the shaman theme well. There's no doubt in my mind that trickster and warrior will be well served, but shaman has me worried. Just hoping that they get plenty of charms that play into Luna's thematics - she's just as, if not more important to her chosen than the Unconquered Sun is to his in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Hopefully if they're making Totem more important they'll make it easier to actually get the totem you want. Having to start with Essence 3, Stamina 4 and two knacks just to give a No Moon a butterfly totem is ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>Knacks other than Humble Mouse Shape or Towering Beast Form didn't expand totem choices. Also, some of the larger butterflies were probably in reach of Humble Mouse Shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:50:57-08:00","id":52496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52486#post52486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it can be Motive-Dissecting Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Why</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we got confirmation on that dying earlier than anything else. I heard that it clashed with developer vision for the distinctness of magical weapons. </div> </div> </div>I can see a single alternate form being one whole evocation, at least. We're probably not going to see any easy innate artifact power or evocation which allows it to assume any and all possible forms, no.<br /> <br /> But if a moonsilver sword cannot shapeshift into a different weapon form at all, what's the point?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither of them are really all that physical, though. </div> </div> </div>I think physicality is going to be more of a recurring theme than a universal requirement. If all Lunar Charms required some blatant personal transformation, how would they be different from the organ-based Liminals or cybernetic-dependent Alchemicals?<br /> <br /> Perhaps physicality is also going to be emphasized through the effects that Lunars don't get, like the power to conjure external sensory illusions. To make people see things falsely, they'll probably have to rely on words and physical props. Or, rather the scalpel approach, the hammer method of driving others mad enough to hallucinate wildly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Knacks other than Humble Mouse Shape or Towering Beast Form didn't expand totem choices. Also, some of the larger butterflies were probably in reach of Humble Mouse Shape. </div> </div> </div>I suppose if one wants a butterfly for a spirit shape, having a giant butterfly form to start with isn't all that bad, especially if you can acquire the ability to shrink it whenever you want.<br /> <br /> But who wants to be a pygmy elephant or tyrant lizard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:04:26-08:00","id":52501,"title":"","content":"If Illusion is no longer Lunar territory, then does mean the Changing Moon anima is getting changed? I hope not, I like that one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:22:36-08:00","id":52512,"title":"","content":"I actually fully expect Moonlight Hunt to survive in an Essence 5 appropriate way. It's simply too interesting a hook for what are essentially the mobility exalts to give it up simply because it's previously been problematic. I think explaining it as time manipulation is kind of silly. You can easily just say &quot;they become so much faster&quot; and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> I don't think most of the existing Lunar perfect effect Charms will return, just because most of them were so poorly written they produced a lot of grumbling and griping. Which is somewhat disappointing, bluntly. Most of them are interesting and unique in ways that many other perfect Charms simply were not.<br /> <br /> I don't expect to see any of the lairing Charms return for Lunars, with the possible exception of one that simply carves out a temporary safe place anywhere for the Lunar to hide in while they rest. I think Wyld-keyworded Charms in general will see the axe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:07:00-08:00","id":52568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52496#post52496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Why</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a JoJo's Bizarre Adventure reference (Series 5)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can see a single alternate form being one whole evocation, at least. We're probably not going to see any easy innate artifact power or evocation which allows it to assume any and all possible forms, no.<br /> <br /> But if a moonsilver sword cannot shapeshift into a different weapon form at all, what's the point? </div> </div> </div>The point is that it's a legendary sword made to be a legendary sword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think physicality is going to be more of a recurring theme than a universal requirement. If all Lunar Charms required some blatant personal transformation, how would they be different from the organ-based Liminals or cybernetic-dependent Alchemicals? </div> </div> </div>Sleek and natural instead of a grotesque patchwork or obviously mechanical implants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps physicality is also going to be emphasized through the effects that Lunars don't get, like the power to conjure external sensory illusions. To make people see things falsely, they'll probably have to rely on words and physical props. Or, rather the scalpel approach, the hammer method of driving others mad enough to hallucinate wildly. </div> </div> </div>Well, you could make people hallucinate, but it would involve turning into a particular type of amphibian and eating a whole lot of a specific type of ant. And getting licked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose if one wants a butterfly for a spirit shape, having a giant butterfly form to start with isn't all that bad, especially if you can acquire the ability to shrink it whenever you want.<br /> <br /> But who wants to be a pygmy elephant or tyrant lizard? </div> </div> </div>Mouse-sized butterflies wouldn't necessarily be very giant. As for the opposite side, I could see reasons for either, but I do generally advocate that the totem should be exempt from Knack requirements. There should be no expansion of choice, just offer the whole wide variety up front and require the expansions to get other shapes. You also avoid the ambiguity of what you can choose as a totem, and don't have to write in which ones, specifically, expand the choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:44:10-08:00","id":52665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52512#post52512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually fully expect Moonlight Hunt to survive in an Essence 5 appropriate way. It's simply too interesting a hook for what are essentially the mobility exalts to give it up simply because it's previously been problematic. I think explaining it as time manipulation is kind of silly. You can easily just say &quot;they become so much faster&quot; and leave it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that Moonlight Hunt was a space-warping teleportation Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think most of the existing Lunar perfect effect Charms will return, just because most of them were so poorly written they produced a lot of grumbling and griping. Which is somewhat disappointing, bluntly. Most of them are interesting and unique in ways that many other perfect Charms simply were not. </div> </div> </div>Beast Spirit Defense was a Heavenly Guardian Defense you could use barehanded, Flowing Body Evasion was essentially no different from Seven Shadow Evasion, and there was no perfect soak. That leaves the &quot;Defend Other perfect defense&quot;, but even THAT used the Solar Flaws of Invulnerability just like the rest of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:48:30-08:00","id":52670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52665#post52665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that Moonlight Hunt was a space-warping teleportation Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is from a fluff standpoint. It doesn't have to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52665#post52665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast Spirit Defense was a Heavenly Guardian Defense you could use barehanded, Flowing Body Evasion was essentially no different from Seven Shadow Evasion, and there was no perfect soak. That leaves the &quot;Defend Other perfect defense&quot;, but even THAT used the Solar Flaws of Invulnerability just like the rest of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I waste time talking about combat-oriented perfects? Don't be silly.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about their other, more intriguing perfect-alike effects. Things like Furious Hound Pursuit and Eye of the Cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:27:39-08:00","id":52721,"title":"","content":"I don't see why you would get rid of illusion effects.<br /> Lunars whole Man and Monster dichotomy thing meshes nicely with &quot;the moon is associated with insanity&quot; powers, and inducing hallucinations, nightmares, and madness is definitely a thing I want my lunar shamans and tricksters (hell, maybe even warriors) to do. I can definitely see tying those powers more closely to the self, though: making oneself an object of nightmares or of obsession or of hallucinations. I like the idea of a Lunar being able to walk up to you in the shape of your beloved grandmother, carrying a pie that smells just like the pie she used to make even though Granny died twenty years ago. I'm not so interested in a Lunar being able to conjure a palace out of moonlight and gossamer...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:45:19-08:00","id":52731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52721#post52721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why you would get rid of illusion effects.<br /> Lunars whole Man and Monster dichotomy thing meshes nicely with &quot;the moon is associated with insanity&quot; powers, and inducing hallucinations, nightmares, and madness is definitely a thing I want my lunar shamans and tricksters (hell, maybe even warriors) to do. I can definitely see tying those powers more closely to the self, though: making oneself an object of nightmares or of obsession or of hallucinations. I like the idea of a Lunar being able to walk up to you in the shape of your beloved grandmother, carrying a pie that smells just like the pie she used to make even though Granny died twenty years ago. I'm not so interested in a Lunar being able to conjure a palace out of moonlight and gossamer...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmares are nightmares and something that a Lunar breathes into you while you're sleeping. Possibly, in the context of physicality, in the form of a small, phantom night creature made of Essence.<br /> <br /> Pleasant dreams.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Odd vapors are still plenty physical, though, and physically becoming something monstrous is always game.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:15:00-08:00","id":52898,"title":"","content":"In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:20:03-08:00","id":52902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52898#post52898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Medusa's Head Defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:23:22-08:00","id":52905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52898#post52898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rewrote that Charm with Second Edition mechanics in such a way that it was mechanically distinct from anything else they had and yet only as modestly powerful as Cunning Porcupine Defense. Significantly simpler and much less potentially broken than the First Edition mechanics.<br /> <br /> I kept the name, but I allowed it to express itself as rats made of shadows leaping out of your shadow or murders of crows flying out of your sleeves, and things like that.<br /> <br /> If you don't get us this Charm, and if environmental hazards still exist in some form, I can do it for Third Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:27:58-08:00","id":52911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52902#post52902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medusa's Head Defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in close contention with Hella Snakes Prana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T19:03:53-08:00","id":52926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52911#post52911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is in close contention with Hella Snakes Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't give a fuck what it's named in the book. This is what the charm is called.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T19:05:39-08:00","id":52927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52911#post52911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has just given me the strangest urge: Next time i run a game, I want to make a Lunar NPC/ antagonist and give them this charm.<br /> Then, i'm going to keep having him do stuff that causes other NPC's to keep mentioning them, for reasons, but the PC's won't get to actually see him.<br /> And anytime they ask about this never-seen person, all they'll get is:<br /> &quot;He's a right slippery one that one&quot;<br /> &quot;Known to wriggle out of all sorts&quot;<br /> &quot;Went to diner with him, definitely got a mouth bigger than his eyes&quot;<br /> &quot;Never piss that fella off, got quite the forked tongue. It'll end up poisoning more than just you reputation i'll tell you now&quot;<br /> &quot;Got a real toothy grin&quot;<br /> <br /> And then, when they finally get to meet him, BAM arms turn into snakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T20:02:50-08:00","id":52954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52911#post52911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is in close contention with Hella Snakes Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am disappointed that Indiana Jonesing Method wasn't a frontrunner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T21:02:28-08:00","id":52979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52898#post52898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I didn't even remember that. It is, admittedly, pretty great. I had a Lunar in a homebrew game whose soak effect was fluffed as turning parts of his body into thick masses of feathers, but snakes are <i>pretty hard to beat</i>. Though it makes me wonder -- it's very specific for a modern Lunar effect, and my instinct would be to refluff it as &quot;some kind of small animal&quot; so you can use spiders or rats or whatever. On the other hand, maybe that kind of specificity will return in 3e? I can see cases for and against, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T03:26:01-08:00","id":53100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52898#post52898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Lunars had a Charm called Snake Head Defense that let them turn various parts of the body into just a fuckload of snakes as a defensive countermeasure. You can expect me to brandish my freelancing knives with as much fury as I can bring to bear to get that effect into 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Probably needs a cooler name, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here? This has me more confident in the direction of 3E Lunars than anything else I've seen written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T03:33:10-08:00","id":53102,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Lunars could still have Charms, old or new, which are premised on modifications to their own personal psychological state in a variety of forms, without it necessarily being an actual overt neurological modification or an idea that they can necessarily inflict psychedelic effects on other people, just because that seems suitable to some of the phrasing the developers have used for them in addition to their physicality and as something to draw from Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T04:04:52-08:00","id":53113,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a charm where I can turn into a swarm of.... something, Bees, Hornets, butterflies, any type small, flying creature, to dodge stuff. Safety in Numbers Understanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T04:36:12-08:00","id":53118,"title":"","content":"I expect to see Deadly Beastman Transformation, along with many others from first edition. Just, you know, not broken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:18:18-08:00","id":53176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53113#post53113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a charm where I can turn into a swarm of.... something, Bees, Hornets, butterflies, any type small, flying creature, to dodge stuff. Safety in Numbers Understanding?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the classic Emerald Circle Sorcery spells though.<br /> Also how does it really benefit you more than turning you into one of those things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:56:35-08:00","id":53235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parallel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53176#post53176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one of the classic Emerald Circle Sorcery spells though.<br /> Also how does it really benefit you more than turning you into one of those things?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks cooler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:19:48-08:00","id":53252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parallel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53176#post53176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one of the classic Emerald Circle Sorcery spells though.<br /> Also how does it really benefit you more than turning you into one of those things?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably much, much cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:28:27-08:00","id":53260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52501#post52501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Illusion is no longer Lunar territory, then does mean the Changing Moon anima is getting changed? I hope not, I like that one...</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the mechanics are rewritten to actually reflect what the power does, I'm fine with it. Personally though, I'd rather it just gave you an aura of trustworthiness (which is it's only mechanical effect right now) or something and save the actual disguise powers for charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:40:57-08:00","id":53296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53260#post53260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the mechanics are rewritten to actually reflect what the power does, I'm fine with it. Personally though, I'd rather it just gave you an aura of trustworthiness (which is it's only mechanical effect right now) or something and save the actual disguise powers for charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, I'd prefer that the effect was stackable with a Trust-Aura Charm available to any Lunar. Changing Moons might be the best tricksters of the bunch, but all Lunars are potentially tricksters, yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:22:29-08:00","id":53332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53113#post53113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a charm where I can turn into a swarm of.... something, Bees, Hornets, butterflies, any type small, flying creature, to dodge stuff. Safety in Numbers Understanding?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean retoolings of the swarm Knacks from Glories: Luna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:38:58-08:00","id":53346,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly interested to see three names from 1e come back (I think they were only in 1e)<br /> - Ferocious Biting Sword (got renamed Ferocious Biting Fang? Tooth? Dunno, but Sword rung better).<br /> - Pulse of the Invisible (just an interesting tactile vibe to their version of AESS).<br /> - Body-Breaking Kata (because I love the name itself really).<br /> <br /> And from 2e, names I like regardless of what effect htey finally have:<br /> - Heron Sheds Rain<br /> - Becoming the Envy of Water<br /> <br /> That's all.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:02:45-08:00","id":53395,"title":"","content":"Really, the idea that shapeshifting Exalts had an Anima power that let them look like other people in a manner that wasn't shapeshifting seems kind of fiddly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:07:23-08:00","id":53400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52911#post52911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is in close contention with Hella Snakes Prana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motherfucking Snakes on this Motherfucking Limb Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:53:36-08:00","id":53428,"title":"","content":"I feel like a broken record every time this topic comes up, but eh. I imagine some revised form of Lunar Blood Shaping Technique, Insidious Lunar Transformation (voluntary and involuntary polymorph respectively), Burgeoning Wyld Affliction (temporary/permanent mutations to others), and Flesh-Sculpting Art (combination healing/disguise) will be back, and hopefully expanded. Also made more easily accessible and more potent, in places (upgrades/repurchases for longer effect durations alone would have been nice).<br /> <br /> Transforming other people just seems a solid fit for the kind of primal mythic space the devs have talked about for Lunars. I can just also see a case against, depending on where the splat is headed. If one of the big EX3 Lunar theses is a variant on, &quot;No, Lunar powers don't directly magically change the world around them, but man can they change themselves in such impressive and multitudinous ways: they're not short on options for changing the world around them in huge and amazing ways,&quot; then I'm not sure those powers will fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:31:40-08:00","id":53461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=52496#post52496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Why</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sluuuurp.*<br /> <br /> You taste like a liar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:42:54-08:00","id":53469,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the number of Lunar charms that are interesting and defining enough to be worth returning as anything close to what they were in previous editions probably comes to about a handful or so, if that. There will likely be charm names that get reused, and there will be charms that occupy the general role of many older charms, but I don't think many things will survive as anything close to what they were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:19:12-08:00","id":53499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53461#post53461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sluuuurp.*<br /> <br /> You taste like a liar.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qA2lj_7xhq8\" target=\"_blank\">ARRIVEDERCI!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:45:08-08:00","id":53542,"title":"","content":"There was 1st ed charm COOLEST OF THEM ALL which let you turn your hands and feet into leopard hands and feet. What amazing powers did it grant the user? Well be sure to be sitted... it gave you a mediocre bonus to climbing... oh and it imposed penalties to any other actions...<br /> <br /> \u200bI hope to never see that shit again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:45:11-08:00","id":53543,"title":"","content":"So, anyone disagree with the idea that Monkey Arm Style and other Mister Fantastic shenanigans might NOT be returning as Lunar tricks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:52:13-08:00","id":53549,"title":"","content":"I disagree. A Charm to increase a Lunar's reach &amp; flexibility is well within theme for them, not to mention dead useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:55:51-08:00","id":53553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53543#post53543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anyone disagree with the idea that Monkey Arm Style and other Mister Fantastic shenanigans might NOT be returning as Lunar tricks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by the double negative, but IIRC it's been heavily implied they're not returning.<br /> <br /> And I feel that, mostly, they aren't a good fit for Lunars -- they don't fit well into the sort of mythological shapeshifting Lunars draw on. I'd prefer for Lunar charms to focus on evoking the thematic and practical associations of their forms (turning into a lion and then stunning people with your mighty roar or invoking your authority as king of the beasts) rather than feeling like they're going for something that ultimately ends with a body-horror amorphous blob. Monkey Arm Style wouldn't be that bad to have, mind, but I don't think it should be the main direction of their charmset.<br /> <br /> (Although those charms weren't common or particularly central to Lunars in 2e, either -- I think people mostly seized on them because there was a lack of other things to grab on to.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:00:55-08:00","id":53559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53553#post53553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by the double negative, but IIRC it's been heavily implied they're not returning.<br /> <br /> And I feel that, mostly, they aren't a good fit for Lunars -- they don't fit well into the sort of mythological shapeshifting Lunars draw on. I'd prefer for Lunar charms to focus on evoking the thematic and practical associations of their forms (turning into a lion and then stunning people with your mighty roar or invoking your authority as king of the beasts) rather than feeling like they're going for something that ultimately ends with a body-horror amorphous blob. Monkey Arm Style wouldn't be that bad to have, mind, but I don't think it should be the main direction of their charmset.<br /> <br /> (Although those charms weren't common or particularly central to Lunars in 2e, either -- I think people mostly seized on them because there was a lack of other things to grab on to.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of much cooler ways for one to extend their reach within the Lunar paradigm than just shooting it out all floppy noodle Plastic Man style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:09:47-08:00","id":53561,"title":"","content":"It would seem odd to me that Lunars have Charms to directly enhance their Dexterity, transform a body part into a snake, and alter their size through DBT, but don't have a Charm to stretch a limb out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:10:59-08:00","id":53563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53543#post53543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anyone disagree with the idea that Monkey Arm Style and other Mister Fantastic shenanigans might NOT be returning as Lunar tricks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am cool with the long-arm Dhalsim stuff. I think it'd be a little odd if Lunars couldn't do that. I don't know that it should be a general competence, but in 2e it was basically the way Lunars did Iron Raptor and I think that's a pretty reasonable niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:37:09-08:00","id":53587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53559#post53559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of much cooler ways for one to extend their reach within the Lunar paradigm than just shooting it out all floppy noodle Plastic Man style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it involve one or more of 666 beast shapes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:26:52-08:00","id":53916,"title":"","content":"I, too, REALLY hope they don't throw away the whole &quot;Feint&quot; Charm tree. It's cool. On a side note, though, I found the idea that Lunars rock at dual (Or tri, or quad, or what-have-you) wielding to be neat, and I also sort of liked those Lunar Charms that let them do that. So I hope that doesn't go out the window, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/792-karpattata","name":"Karpattata","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:07:54-08:00","id":53996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53559#post53559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of much cooler ways for one to extend their reach within the Lunar paradigm than just shooting it out all floppy noodle Plastic Man style.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as we avoid prehensile tongues we're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:20:43-08:00","id":54007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53996#post53996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we avoid prehensile tongues we're good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prehensile-tailed then<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=Xz3btMhdQ6Y#t=235\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=Xz3btMhdQ6Y#t=235\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=Xz3btMhdQ6Y#t=235\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=Xz3btMhdQ6Y#t=235 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:31:25-08:00","id":54016,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the love for the Butterfly + Noun tree, since every posts concerning those charm is some variant of &quot;I just wish Butterfly Eyes/Dicks/Boobs were more awesome&quot; I guess people just got mesmerize by the charm's name then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:28:36-08:00","id":54054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=53996#post53996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we avoid prehensile tongues we're good.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just want Lunars to stop getting all the ladies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:02:47-08:00","id":54358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54016#post54016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the love for the Butterfly + Noun tree, since every posts concerning those charm is some variant of &quot;I just wish Butterfly Eyes/Dicks/Boobs were more awesome&quot; I guess people just got mesmerize by the charm's name then.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was going to go down the list of the Charms and point out how very right you were, but the more I look at them in light of a new system, the more potential I'm seeing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Butterfly Eyes Defense sucked in practice, but if one could find a worthwhile mechanical representation in the new system, I can see how the basic concept is cool. It doesn't need to rely on spectral illusions, just preternatural talent at faking and misdirection.<br /> <br /> Butterfly Eyes Tread is pathetically narrow as written, but if it were revised to allow the Lunar to distract his targets attention from anything and everything except the Lunar himself, or at least other possible directions than only &quot;down&quot;, it would be really sweet. And again, no need for visual illusions, because the Lunar is relying on that Majestic God-Body thing to hold someone's attention, in combination with the misdirection talents he developed for Butterfly Eyes Defense. (However, careful consideration should go into how this Charm's concept compares against the concept of False Burrow Pursuit, and whether the Lunars need both Charms.)<br /> <br /> Butterfly Eyes Fist is still completely within the same thematic realm as the first two; still no spectral illusions to toss out of the picture. On the mechanical side, this would actually be a really awesome Charm to use as a Finishing Move within the momentum-based new combat system, since it's very binary and potentially very powerful -- either it doesn't work at all, or it allows you to dictate the other character's next action.<br /> <br /> Mystic Butterfly Fraud, however, doesn't belong. It makes no sense as a Supplemental Charm, and its function can already be fulfilled by Mirror Sight Dismay (or a cousin Charm which works in reverse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:09:12-08:00","id":54363,"title":"","content":"The names <i>are </i>good, but also it's just really cool to have a Manipulation tree based on psyche play in combat. That's the kind of thing I like to see in Manipulation, and in general &quot;mind games&quot; powers are super fun when done well in combat minigames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:13:28-08:00","id":54364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54016#post54016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the love for the Butterfly + Noun tree, since every posts concerning those charm is some variant of &quot;I just wish Butterfly Eyes/Dicks/Boobs were more awesome&quot; I guess people just got mesmerize by the charm's name then.</div> </div> </div> </div>BUTTERFLY EYES CHARMS<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b><b>:</b> Illusion, Authorial<br /> <br /> None can deny the prowess of the Chosen of Luna. Any reader who reads any charm beginning with the name 'butterfly eyes' becomes convinced that they are reading an interesting and useful charm. This effect is unnatural mental influence costing 1 WP to resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:20:38-08:00","id":54370,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I have a permanent Defense Against Terrible Charms Method going. No Willpower for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:31:31-08:00","id":54376,"title":"","content":"Remember that World-Weaver Charm TDO teased us about in the recent past? It would let Lunars change the way gravity worked within a specific territory; as in, intensity (strong/weak) or direction (down/sideways).<br /> <br /> Preeeeetty sure that's going to be a Getimian thing, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:35:16-08:00","id":54380,"title":"","content":"More seriously, I think it's just that there's a kneejerk reaction on the part of fans whenever &quot;should your favorite splat have <i>this?</i>&quot; comes up to say yes as loud as possible unless it's something that clearly and obviously violates their theme.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that whatever charms Lunars lose in the edition change, they'll get new stuff to replace. That's why I said that in my view there's maybe a dozen charms worth keeping, if that -- the others are often not terrible or anything, but I feel that they could probably get better stuff starting mostly from scratch than from trying to revise the old things, and there are very few charms that are so iconic that I'd say &quot;if they lack this charm, they don't feel like Lunars to me!&quot;<br /> <br /> (Whereas there's, say, a bunch of iconic charms in the Sidereal charmset, which I expect will be adopted in some fashion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:43:12-08:00","id":54385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54380#post54380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember that whatever charms Lunars lose in the edition change, they'll get new stuff to replace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do intend to start a thread soon about what new Charms we think Lunars might get, in regards to the &quot;barbarian shaman trickster&quot; themes.<br /> <br /> But I think this thread still serves a purpose, and it's easier to imagine what won't return than to imagine what will replace the cast-offs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I said that in my view there's maybe a dozen charms worth keeping, if that -- the others are often not terrible or anything, but I feel that they could probably get better stuff starting mostly from scratch than from trying to revise the old things, and there are very few charms that are so iconic that I'd say &quot;if they lack this charm, they don't feel like Lunars to me!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Listing which of those vanishingly few Lunar Charms you think belong on that list would be an appropriate use of this thread.<br /> <br /> For me... well, someone already mentioned Blood-Reshaping Technique. If Lunars cannot turn other people into animals, something is terribly, terribly wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm also happy that Vance is dedicated to bringing back Snake Head Defense (with better mechanics).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:34:36-08:00","id":54420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54370#post54370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I have a permanent Defense Against Terrible Charms Method going. No Willpower for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My defensive method is a complete loathing of phantasmal forces and related illusion effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:32:36-08:00","id":54450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54385#post54385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me... well, someone already mentioned Blood-Reshaping Technique. If Lunars cannot turn other people into animals, something is terribly, terribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I can kinda see them not having the others I mentioned (Insidious Lunar Transformation aside), but lacking something like this'd just be straight-up bewildering to me. Like, I'd find it an oddly specific and questionable splat direction that captures man-beast dualism the way Lunars do and leaves applying that to others completely out of the equation.<br /> <br /> Then again, might mostly be me; I've always had an interest in that sort of magic. I'd quite happily play a character who was about pretty much nothing beyond transforming people and creatures (and things, to a degree).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:41:14-08:00","id":54452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54385#post54385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also happy that Vance is dedicated to bringing back Snake Head Defense (with better mechanics).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, you can count on me to be an advocate of anything that involves turning into a bunch of snakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:05:15-08:00","id":54466,"title":"","content":"So, Viper Pantsing Technique is a &quot;go&quot; then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:31:53-08:00","id":54473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54452#post54452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general rule, you can count on me to be an advocate of anything that involves turning into a bunch of snakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if turning into a snake never helps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:34:13-08:00","id":54474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54473#post54473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if turning into a snake never helps?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine. Turning into a snake basically <i>always</i> helps. I cannot imagine a single scenario where it wouldn't. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">except for, you know. doorknobs.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:57:15-08:00","id":54523,"title":"","content":"I, personally, hate stretchy powers. I don't want to see them go away; I'm sure there is plenty of space for it and plenty of people who love... Plastic Man... Elongating Man... Mr Fantastic... Captain Forenoodles whatever. But please... not as the whole paradigm. It's all I ask.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Unless they're elongating snakes. Because I'm all for elongating snakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:33:09-08:00","id":54545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54364#post54364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUTTERFLY EYES CHARMS<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b><b>:</b> Illusion, Authorial<br /> <br /> None can deny the prowess of the Chosen of Luna. Any reader who reads any charm beginning with the name 'butterfly eyes' becomes convinced that they are reading an interesting and useful charm. This effect is unnatural mental influence costing 1 WP to resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have Righteous Lion Defense keyed to &quot;My Dignity,&quot; so I'm afraid this doesn't work on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T07:38:54-08:00","id":54653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54466#post54466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Viper Pantsing Technique is a &quot;go&quot; then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the prerequisite for Mammoth Equine Trouser Snake Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:04:12-08:00","id":54668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foorish Shamurai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54523#post54523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, hate stretchy powers. I don't want to see them go away; I'm sure there is plenty of space for it and plenty of people who love... Plastic Man... Elongating Man... Mr Fantastic... Captain Forenoodles whatever. But please... not as the whole paradigm. It's all I ask.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Unless they're elongating snakes. Because I'm all for elongating snakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freud would have a field day with this.<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I think &quot;stretchy powers&quot; work for Lunars. They can transform their bodies in numerous ways, so it fits perfectly. The trick is wording it in the book and imagining it in your mind as not looking like Plastic Man/Mr. Fantastic. Think of it more like bones and muscles stretching &amp; growing, perhaps additional joints popping up as the Lunar elongates her limb, or perhaps her arm does become more elastic, but in turn it slithers like a snake or twists like the leg of a spider.<br /> <br /> If all you can think of is superheroes when you see a Charm that offers the ability to stretch a limb, then that's not the fault of the Charm itself. There are numerous Charms reminiscent of comic book superpowers, but if they're in-theme and useful, then there's no reason not to include them in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:42:08-08:00","id":54685,"title":"","content":"It's like people didn't read a word of what I had to say regarding rubber-man powers on the last page. Certainly, no one's bothering to challenge my points. Very frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:58:29-08:00","id":54697,"title":"","content":"I see no such post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:12:41-08:00","id":54709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54474#post54474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning into a snake basically <i>always</i> helps. I cannot imagine a single scenario where it wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god. Snake-based seduction.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey baby, ever wonder what a forked tongue feels like?&quot; =(<br /> <br /> Although, it would be hilarious seeing a snake trying to use craft to forge a sword or build a cabinet.<br /> <br /> Edit: Let's see, what other things would turning into a snake not help? Hm...<br /> <br /> Pole-vaulting<br /> Olympic long jump<br /> Changing a wheel<br /> Driving a car<br /> Spelling bees &quot;The word is &quot;telemetry.&quot;&quot; &quot;Ssssss-&quot; &quot;Disqualified.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 01-21-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:20:24-08:00","id":54713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54709#post54709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Let's see, what other things would turning into a snake not help? Hm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Calming down an ophidiophobe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:24:40-08:00","id":54717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54713#post54713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calming down an ophidiophobe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to convince someone you're not a snake...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:29:54-08:00","id":54721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54717#post54717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to convince someone you're not a snake...</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to be an oil salesman.<br /> <br /> (also <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xr37BJA3cLI\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Snaken Boo, what's the matter with you~&quot;</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:22:48-08:00","id":54776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54697#post54697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no such post.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean this one? On the first page like I said?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=51978#post51978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think Monkey Arm Style will return?<br /> <br /> The hatewheel has expressed contempt for and exasperation with &quot;elastic body&quot; powers, but the hamster has said that something like the elastic body Shintai from Kindred of the East is not out of the question (though he didn't say for which splats).<br /> <br /> Monkey Arm Style does seem problematic for me in regards to the Lunar Exalted. The Alchemical Exalted have an excellent reason for an extending arm feature to NOT include the option to extend one's other appendages or body parts, which allows for it to be a properly self-contained Charm, with an entirely separate cousin Charm that extends the Alchemical's legs. Easy to design, balance and write.<br /> <br /> But unlike the Alchemical Exalted, the Lunar Exalted can easily switch back and forth between forms that technically don't have any arms at all, or at least where their arms would be legs or wings. It's also harder (though admittedly not impossible) to justify why a Lunar Charm which extends an arm (which could be a foreleg) doesn't also extend the Lunar's legs. And a Charm that allows an Exalt to extend both arms and legs is an extremely complicated mess to design, balance and write.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is, I think the Lunar Exalted may already be so variable in form that giving them &quot;elastic body&quot; Charms might not actually over-complicate things. Whereas Exalts who don't have the innate power to easily assume any inhuman form can freely accept such tricks into their arsenal (especially the Liminal and Alchemical Exalted).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:28:39-08:00","id":54782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54420#post54420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My defensive method is a complete loathing of phantasmal forces and related illusion effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did already point out how only Mystic Butterfly Fraud works like that (and how it's the only irredeemable concept among the four). The three preceding Charms really are about feinting, misdirection, distraction and fakery through body language and actions.<br /> <br /> I don't know about any Charms in Lords of Creation, but fuck Lords of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:45:54-08:00","id":54795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54776#post54776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean this one? On the first page like I said?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54685#post54685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like people didn't read a word of what I had to say regarding rubber-man powers <b>on the last page</b>. Certainly, no one's bothering to challenge my points. Very frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never change, Tornado Wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> To address what you wrote on the first page, I do think there is merit to a Monkey Arm Style Charm for one's legs where the Lunars are concerned, but I also agree that a singular Charm capable of allowing a Lunar to extend any limb is rather problematic. However, I don't see the idea that a Lunar can change form into animals without arms (or similar appendages) as a problem in and of itself. There are always going to be Charms that are less useful in certain situations. A Solar with a Melee Charm can't use it unless he's got a melee weapon in his hand, after all. So the idea that in certain instances a Lunar can't use his limb-extending Charm seems a non-issue to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:01:15-08:00","id":54807,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see my mistake. When I wrote it, I used the word &quot;last&quot; to mean &quot;the one before this one&quot;, as in &quot;last week&quot;.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't think to call the latest/current page the last one unless it was dead or locked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54795#post54795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the idea that a Lunar can change form into animals without arms (or similar appendages) as a problem in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that Monkey Arm Technique should just not work at all with wings, though it can work with arms, legs, tails, tentacles, and probably necks and horns?<br /> <br /> And going back to tails, ignore monkey tails for a moment and ask yourself how it works with fish or whale tails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:53:28-08:00","id":54839,"title":"","content":"Don't put words in my mouth. I just don't see the fact that it might not be applicable with certain animal shapes as a serious enough issue to warrant not including the Charm in the book at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:57:11-08:00","id":56514,"title":"","content":"How about this? Could you see Conan using Monkey Arm Style or any of Mister Fantastic's other tricks?<br /> <br /> I just don't think &quot;extending arm&quot; fits the &quot;barbarian&quot; aesthetic that 3rd Edition Lunar Charms are supposed to evoke. It fits very well with the mechanical Alchemical Exalted or the unnatural Liminal Exalted. I could imagine Frankenstein's monster tinkering with his anatomy to include inhuman organs and features as easily as I can see a cyborg with a telescoping punch attack.<br /> <br /> But Conan would sooner hurl the very image of his bestial soul at his enemies to maul them from a distance, or perhaps blast them off their feet with a mighty animal roar. Or else simply lift and fling a large rock at them as if it were a sling stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:43:54-08:00","id":56540,"title":"","content":"I don't exactly see Conan transforming into a mouse or turning parts of his body into snakes, but whatever.<br /> <br /> While I don't disagree that Alchemicals and Liminals would be likely to have such a power (the Prometheans, on whom the Liminals are loosely based, actually do have a limb-extending power), I don't think it's out-of-theme for Lunars to have it as well. There's lots of different types of barbarians, and a trickster who can elongate a limb to pickpocket someone, grab a high tree branch from the ground to escape, or perhaps even perform a rear attack doesn't sound ludicrous to me the way it seems to sound to you. Mainly it seems to be that I don't automatically envision Mr. Fantastic when imagining how a Charm like that would look &amp; work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T21:25:52-08:00","id":56571,"title":"","content":"In the vein of the Snake Defense Charm I would really like to see one where the Lunar turns any damage taken into scarabs that fly off from him and then start skittering back to him in order to heal the wounds that spawned them, unless killed before they get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1687-draken","name":"Draken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1687_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T02:09:49-08:00","id":56630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=56514#post56514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this? Could you see Conan using Monkey Arm Style or any of Mister Fantastic's other tricks?<br /> <br /> I just don't think &quot;extending arm&quot; fits the &quot;barbarian&quot; aesthetic that 3rd Edition Lunar Charms are supposed to evoke. It fits very well with the mechanical Alchemical Exalted or the unnatural Liminal Exalted. I could imagine Frankenstein's monster tinkering with his anatomy to include inhuman organs and features as easily as I can see a cyborg with a telescoping punch attack.<br /> <br /> But Conan would sooner hurl the very image of his bestial soul at his enemies to maul them from a distance, or perhaps blast them off their feet with a mighty animal roar. Or else simply lift and fling a large rock at them as if it were a sling stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think it fits. Others think it does.<br /> <br /> Whether it makes it into 3e is outside the control of either party, so why continue to argue about whether it's thematically appropriate to a splat nobody knows the thematics of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T05:03:15-08:00","id":56665,"title":"","content":"I actually like the stretchy powers, There is design space for them, they could be body horror like Tomes from X-Files or creative slingshoting limbs like Luffy or Dhalsim. I can see someone having a starfish or a leech totem having powers to stretch.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/_DpAvG8xujGs/TNgCnRcJoxI/AAAAAAAAATM/NtkHyIYjFc0/s1600/IMGP0286Document%2BName2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T07:40:52-08:00","id":57425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=54709#post54709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Let's see, what other things would turning into a snake not help? Hm...<br /> <br /> Pole-vaulting</div> </div> </div> </div>Donkey Kong Country disagrees!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:07:58-08:00","id":57441,"title":"","content":"If stretchy powers do no return in 3rd Edition, the Terrorists will have won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:44:56-08:00","id":57476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=57441#post57441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If stretchy powers do no return in 3rd Edition, the Terrorists will have won.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus, Lunars will win against the Realm. You heard it here first, folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:10:50-08:00","id":57526,"title":"","content":"When that proposed rewrite of Monkey Arm Style was given, I had images of the Slender Man.<br /> <br /> Who doesn't actually apparently stretch his limbs, it's just that they sometimes happen to be unnaturally long and jointed.<br /> <br /> Also kind of that bit in Twilight Princess when Link first comes up to the Twilight Realm, and the arm of one of the beasts shoots out to drag him in.<br /> <br /> Stuff like ropy, jointed arms, big orangutan kinds of arms (without necessarily actually transforming into animal arms), they still feel aesthetically suitable.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they'd be mechanically distinct from Luffy or Plastic Man style stretching, but I don't think that matters much.<br /> <br /> I also think of Coyote from Gunnerkrigg Court style stretching, which is a bit beyond ropy limbs but also feels short of elastic person style.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's not barbarian, but I feel it's very &quot;freaky beast in the woods&quot;, and still has the &quot;rough, unpolished&quot; aesthetic.<br /> <br /> There was also that stuff with the spirit in the first fight in Legend of Korra. That thing moved more like protoplasm than elastic, I think; less stretching and more flowing. Put a weapon on the end of its far reaching limbs, and that's part of how I can imagine a Lunar swordfighter being distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T16:38:38-08:00","id":57743,"title":"","content":"You can go pretty far with limb extension and the like before it leaves the realm of &quot;body mastery&quot; and becomes &quot;shapeshifting&quot;. When a snake unhinges its jaw or an octopus hides in a small crevice, it's not shapeshifting, and it's definitely not Plastic Man. In real life, your ability to stretch and flex your limbs is something that is partly dependent on the body you're born with and can be further augmented with training, and &quot;stretch your arm to double its length&quot; is the same kind of natural extrapolation of this as &quot;jump 50 feet into the air&quot; is of jumping ability.<br /> <br /> More than anyone else, Lunars are <i>bodily</i>: they have amazing bodies and an unequaled ability to control and refine them. There are a fair number of stretchiness/flexibility powers that fall under that umbrella, and while published charms obviously need to balance a number of factors including &quot;does this look stupid&quot;, I think Lunars should be able to do most of those things if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T16:45:29-08:00","id":57744,"title":"","content":"Another way I can think of to have a reach extension Charm manifest is just wuxia level agility and body control. As long as the range is not dramatically long I can see it coming off as something like a Lunar martial artist hopping up, clamping his feet around a pole or his planted weapon and holding himself up horizontally and punching out to the end of his entire body's length.<br /> <br /> Then of course he holds the position for a moment and smiles cockily at his opponent. I'm totally channeling the Monkey King right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:00:21-07:00","id":102297,"title":"","content":"Sense-Borrowing Method. Do you think it will return?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I was never entirely sure why the Lunar Exalted had this in the first place. The Dragon-Blooded had it before them, and it made sense given the Terrestrial emphasis on team-work and buffing effects.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it fits the &quot;physical, stylistically barbarian&quot; aesthetic that the developers are going for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby"