</div> </div> </div>Still better than almost every 1e Lunar Charm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:20:06-07:00","id":103667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=102353#post102353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect that one that lets you urinate ale will return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn straight it will. Scorpion and Toad Represent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T16:58:31-07:00","id":103720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/25163-what-lunar-charms-do-you-expect-will-or-will-not-return?p=57441#post57441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If stretchy powers do no return in 3rd Edition, the Terrorists will have won.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Alex Mercer: No.<br /> <br /> Nor Carnage, the T-1000, or Twelve from Street Fighter, all of which are variations on Reed Richards and the Plastic Man when you boil them down. Fuck those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so &quot;rubberman, limb-stretchiness&quot; is another feature moving from Lunars to Getimians or Liminals?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the T-1000, and the archetypal genius of Reed Richards, I despise pretty much everything about &quot;stretchy guy&quot; characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The terrorists (that is, the Lunar Exalted) have won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:37:07-07:00","id":176127,"title":"","content":"If Charisma is supposed to be the Attribute one uses for social influence made with utter sincerity, then there are a number of Charisma Charms I don't see returning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Perfect Fear Scent and Terrifying Lust Infliction:</b> These impose opinions which might be radically different from your own. A proper Charisma Charm would instead key off your own beliefs; for example, if you were trying to persuade someone to adopt your own beliefs, you might add (or bonus) a dice bonus equal to the strength of the Intimacy you wanted to impose. The same Charm would also make you a better salesman for a product you believe is a great deal for your customer.<br /> <br /> I see these Charms returning as Appearance Charms that enhance the Lunar's seduction and intimidation actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mind-Blanking Fear Technique:</b> Charisma intimidates people through sincerity -- you are absolutely convinced that you can soundly defeat someone and you absolutely will attack if they do not back off. But Charisma is not about magnifying the threat you pose beyond your actual ability, which is where &quot;terrify someone into laser-guided amnesia&quot; would seem to fit. In fact, rather than a overly-specific Charm about making someone forget a memory, why not have a Manipulation Charm that lets the Lunar alter memories in general? Robert Vance wrote Memory-Spinning Gossamer Couture, which does just that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Lunar Charisma could magnify the impact of a very real demonstration of power. Following Foe-Marking Style could very well be a variant of that Abyssal Charm, Illustrative Overkill Technique. Also known as the <i>Mortal Kombat</i> &quot;Fatality&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unnoticed Confusion Prana, Forgetful Victim Prana, Secret Speech Technique:</b> If Charisma is about honesty, its Charms should not be hiding things. If these return in any form, they'll likely be Manipulation Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Face of the Moon Concealment: </b>This stealth-related Charm could get a pass, since it's about commanding your followers to improve their performance. The fact that the performance is to hide would be immaterial if it weren't for the Manipulation Charms which enhance the Lunar's ability to lead troops through sneaky actions. Either Manipulation needs to leave commanding alone, or Charisma needs to leave even indirect stealth alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Subtle Silver Command:</b> I DO see this Charm returning, but as two separate effects. The first imposes your values on someone else. The other allows you to make social actions against sleeping targets who normally wouldn't be valid targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-21-2014, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}